layout: runbook
title: '0002 · Duplicates share a cause, not a subject'
owner: support desk
status: accepted
reviewed: 2026-10-28
---

**Date:** 28 October 2026 · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)

## Context

Ticket #4471 merged 412 reports on one symptom, a wrong date. They hold separate causes
(see [the split](/kb/incidents/4471-split)). The subject line told us nothing about the cause.

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they share a cause, computed by `causes.ts` from the
tenant's locale and booking form. Subject lines do not decide a merge.

## Consequences

- One ticket per cause, each with its own report count.
- Slower than matching subjects, but a fix closes the right reports.
- Reports the desk reads differently from their cause are footnoted, not hidden.
